{"at": "2026-07-07T21:33:01Z", "commit_ref": "bd18d95", "intent": "spec", "actor": "user", "kind": "input", "content": "The claim-check report flagged 4 item(s) that MUST be fixed before handoff. Apply the following edits to .spec-md:\n\n1. Part B §B.0 Full-surface bays bullet -- REFUTED-POINTER-DRIFT. The claim (`mainView` (`…TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2281`) wires the table canvas and pointer/wheel handlers ONLY for a table bay) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: [inferred existing-artefact claim] Cited line 2281 is the `Ribbon.view { bays = mainBays ... }` call inside `mainControlBar`, NOT `mainView`. `mainView` is actually defined at line 2298; its pointer/wheel handlers are at 2305-2308 and `Border.child (mainTableCanvas model)` at 2311. The named symbol/content is found ~17 lines below the cited line, inside the +/-20 neighborhood (2261-2301). Operator fix: bump 2281 -> 2298.\n2. Part C, dispersive sub-branch paragraph -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (The edit state generalises so unchecking Dispersive restores the constant losslessly (the ladder's existing lossless discipline)) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Trigger 'existing'. Un-anchored: 'the ladder's existing lossless discipline' names no <file>:<symbol>/<line> pointer and no unique class. The other pointers in this paragraph (gyrationComponents :385, modelParameters :291) anchor different claims. The lossless-uncheck mechanic is in fact commented at MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:697 ('the lossless-uncheck mechanic'), but the spec sentence does not cite it. Operator fix: add a concrete pointer.\n3. Part D §D.0, Empty-sample validation bullet -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (The existing tests that save a structurally-empty sample are updated to add content.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Trigger 'existing'. Un-anchored: 'the existing tests that save a structurally-empty sample' names no test file/symbol/line. No pointer to resolve. Operator fix: name the tests to update.\n4. Part E §E.0, Constant-vs-Dispersive presentation bullet -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (Cosmetic — the derived model is unchanged.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Trigger 'unchanged'. Un-anchored: 'the derived model is unchanged' is a design assertion (the presentation change does not alter the derived `MaterialComplexity`) and names no <file>:<symbol>/<line> pointer. No pointer to resolve.\n\nMake NO other edits to .spec-md beyond the items above; every remaining claim in the report was CONFIRMED."}
{"at": "2026-07-07T21:33:01Z", "commit_ref": "bd18d95", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "output", "content": "Applied the 4 claim-check fixes to specs/0035/.spec-md (every other claim was CONFIRMED; no other edits). Each cited pointer was Read-verified before committing.\n\n1. Part B §B.0 full-surface-bays bullet (REFUTED-POINTER-DRIFT): bumped the mainView pointer TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2281 -> :2298. Verified line 2298 is `let mainView`, its pointer/wheel handlers at 2305-2308 and `Border.child (mainTableCanvas model)` at 2311; line 2281 was the `Ribbon.view` call inside `mainControlBar`.\n\n2. Part C dispersive sub-branch (REFUTED-NO-POINTER): replaced the un-anchored \"the ladder's existing lossless discipline\" with a concrete pointer to the lossless-uncheck mechanic commented on `toComplexity` at MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:697 (verified the 696-698 doc comment).\n\n3. Part D §D.0 empty-sample-validation bullet (REFUTED-NO-POINTER): removed the un-anchored \"existing tests that save a structurally-empty sample\" claim. Verified no existing test saves a films-empty/substrate-None sample through validateSample: every seed builds filmStructure (a film, no substrate, ElementId.fs:329) or plateStructure (a substrate, no films, ElementId.fs:337), and the recording-stub Save test bypasses validateSample. Anchored the acceptance to a new negative case beside the blank-name rejection (SampleProxyTests.fs:120) asserting addSample of a films-empty/substrate-None sample returns InvalidSample.\n\n4. Part E §E.0 Constant-vs-Dispersive presentation bullet (REFUTED-NO-POINTER): rephrased the un-anchored \"the derived model is unchanged\" design assertion into a MUST NOT directive anchored to MaterialComplexityEditor.toComplexity (MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:699).\n\nNo CRLF churn: git diff --numstat is identical with and without --ignore-cr-at-eol (15 added / 7 removed).\n"}
